  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1203 AM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nHigh pressure will bring quiet weather to southern Wisconsin\nThursday and Friday, with mostly clear to partly cloudy skies,\nlight winds, and near normal temperatures expected. \nClouds may increase on Saturday ahead of an approaching\nshortwave, though precip chances are currently expected to hold\noff until at least the evening hours.\n\nA series of shortwaves will bring more active weather to the\nforecast area Saturday night through at least early next week.\nIncreased moisture and instability during this period will also\ncontribute to higher chances for showers and storms.\nTemperatures will be near to a bit above normal during this\nperiod, with more humid conditions returning with dewpoints in \nthe 60s to around 70. \n\nDDV",
